{"type":"message","id":"4ccc3b9f","parentId":"1ecaa806","timestamp":"2026-04-11T15:00:43.272Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first bytes are `123,10,32,32,34,99,104,97,116,108,97` which is `{  \"chatla` - that's the JSON content, not the filename! The filename starts with `{` which is very strange. Wait, actually those are the file contents, not the filename bytes.\n\nActually looking at the file `˽��_11.json`, the first bytes being `{` (123) suggests the file content starts with `{`. The filename itself is different.\n\nI need to get the raw filename bytes. Let me use .NET to get the filename bytes directly.","thinkingSignature":"37480fa6e92e272495754e72367727d2f4127cdc01891c960577f0ac4d745e0a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_05pf24w8k7o2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"\n$src = \"F:\\Wechat shuju\\texts\"\n$f = Get-ChildItem $src -File | Select-Object -First 1\n$nameBytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::Default.GetBytes($f.Name)\nWrite-Host \"File: $($f.Name)\"\nWrite-Host \"Name bytes: $($nameBytes | ForEach-Object { '{0:X2}' -f $_ }) -join ' '\"\nWrite-Host \"Name as iso-8859-1: $([System.Text.Encoding]::GetEncoding('iso-8859-1').GetString($nameBytes))\"\nWrite-Host \"Name as gbk: $([System.Text.Encoding]::GetEncoding('gbk').GetString($nameBytes))\"\n\n# 检查前缀字符的byte\n$p = $f.Name.Substring(0,1)\n$pb = [System.Text.Encoding]::Default.GetBytes($p)\nWrite-Host \"First char '$p' bytes: $($pb | ForEach-Object { '{0:X2}' -f $_ })\"\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":12794,"output":362,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45990,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775919633189,"responseId":"0629950fb8a6a15f923ee69b4dde9fc3"}}
