{"type":"message","id":"83e8a984","parentId":"db842099","timestamp":"2026-04-11T15:01:35.376Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No output from the `Where-Object` with `Ⱥ*`. That's because the console display `Ⱥ` is not the actual GBK character. The actual first two bytes of 群 (群聊) need to be determined. Let me look at the raw bytes of a known group chat file. From the first listing, one of the group chat files was `Ⱥ��_1.json`. Let me get the first bytes of that.\n\nActually, I need to use a different approach. Let me look at the first 2 bytes of ALL files and categorize them to understand the encoding pattern.","thinkingSignature":"2baca0dad3ad4201dd932a93e8e3448c2aac317ed460a3d94925c4f9f72fae66"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_njphfafhu9q6_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"\n$src = \"F:\\Wechat shuju\\texts\"\n# 打印所有文件名前2字节（用GBK），看看前缀分布\nGet-ChildItem $src -File | ForEach-Object {\n    $gb = [System.Text.Encoding]::GetEncoding('gbk').GetBytes($_.Name)\n    $first2 = \"$($gb[0].ToString('X2')) $($gb[1].ToString('X2'))\"\n    if ($first2 -ne 'FF FE' -and $first2 -ne 'EF BB') {  # skip BOM\n        Write-Host \"$first2 -> $($_.Name.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(8, $_.Name.Length)))\"\n    }\n} | Sort-Object | Get-Unique\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":16504,"output":308,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49646,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775919686716,"responseId":"06299545221560f837fba1642d9fb38a"}}
