{"type":"message","id":"5b6e8b01","parentId":"f8d386b0","timestamp":"2026-04-11T15:03:26.392Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The GBK encoding of the remaining files is:\n- `CB BD` = 私 (prefix - correct)\n- File length 18 and 17 characters\n\nBut wait, when I did the Copy+Remove earlier, it said \"Copy succeeded\" and \"Remove succeeded\" and the count went from 2 to 1 JSON. But then the file is still there. That's very confusing.\n\nActually wait - I see now: the Copy+Remove test earlier said:\n- \"Source remaining JSON: 1\" after removing 1 JSON file\n- But there are still 2 files: 1 JSON and 1 TXT\n\nSo the JSON was successfully moved (copied then removed), but the TXT is still there. \n\nThe test worked for the JSON file but the subsequent operations failed silently. Now I need to use the GBK prefix approach to identify and remove the remaining files.","thinkingSignature":"c50fcedc3bc6ee0cd8ca9945007a9ef9a377babac4823839d538a70c5a594007"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_v1l5boiwy821_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"\n$src = \"F:\\Wechat shuju\\texts\"\nGet-ChildItem $src -File | ForEach-Object {\n    $gb = [System.Text.Encoding]::GetEncoding('gbk').GetBytes($_.Name)\n    if ($gb[0] -eq 0xCB -and $gb[1] -eq 0xBD) {\n        $ext = $_.Extension\n        $dest = if ($ext -eq '.json') { \"$src\\私聊_json\" } else { \"$src\\私聊_txt\" }\n        $copyResult = Copy-Item -Path $_.FullName -Destination \"$dest\\\" -Force -PassThru\n        $removeResult = Remove-Item -Path $_.FullName -Force -PassThru\n        Write-Host \"OK: $($_.Name) -> $dest\"\n        Write-Host \"  Copy: $copyResult, Remove: $removeResult\"\n    }\n}\nWrite-Host \"Done. Remaining: $((Get-ChildItem $src -File).Count)\"\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":22270,"output":423,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55527,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"c