{"type":"message","id":"0def422c","parentId":"d1390d41","timestamp":"2026-04-11T15:04:12.057Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The files are still there! The Copy succeeded but the Remove didn't actually delete them. This is very strange. Both Copy and Remove said \"OK\" but the files remain. Maybe the issue is that PowerShell is outputting \"Remove OK\" based on the try block succeeding, but Remove-Item actually didn't remove the file.Wait - could it be that the Remove-Item ran BEFORE the Copy-Item was flushed to disk? Like, Copy returns immediately but the file handle isn't released? That seems unlikely.\n\nActually, let me try using `[System.IO.File]::Delete()` instead which is more direct.Or maybe the issue is that the file was already deleted but PowerShell is caching the directory listing. \n\nLet me force a refresh and try again.","thinkingSignature":"f0ce75255f54de68f26a95793dc1dd8e055c7fdfb4cd2ba1a5ec5ef0a81c5b74"},{"type":"text","text":"文件还在，说明 Remove 没真正执行成功。用 .NET 的 File.Delete 试试：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_44ktuekbnqbp_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"\nGet-ChildItem \"F:\\Wechat shuju\\texts\" -File | ForEach-Object {\n    $fullName = $_.FullName\n    Write-Host \"Deleting: $fullName\"\n    [System.IO.File]::Delete($fullName)\n    Write-Host \"Deleted: $([System.IO.File]::Exists($fullName))\"\n}\nWrite-Host \"Remaining: $((Get-ChildItem 'F:\\Wechat shuju\\texts' -File).Count)\"\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":25237,"output":289,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58360,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775919841893,"responseId":"062995e08f0ac5000cc4742b1eaac2d6"}}
